# Browser
# The three-Oblivion-Ring loop (CR 104.4b) at a table, Bot1 a browser page: the game is a draw, and the page says why - the
# game log, which the game-over panel reads its detail from, says the game went round a loop in which every player only
# passed (docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-4). The headless scenario of the same loop says why each Ring's ability has one target
# and why no one can stop it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivion Ring.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivion Ring.Cast
[T7 Bot1.Main2]
? Exile = Oblivion Ring
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
[T9 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oblivion Ring.Cast

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = MandatoryLoop
Turn = 9
Step = Main1
Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Plains; Plains
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
Client.Bot1.Over = true
Client.Bot1.Log.Has = The game is a draw: it went round a loop in which every player only passed (CR 104.4b).
